d stake my life  on it  Erin Moriarty joins us life in prison  does seem very extreme under the  circumstance yes it can I just tell you  that these people really opened up their  lives to us most of the time there were  no attorneys there there were no limits  the kind of questions I could ask I  found them very credible very open and  one of the reasons why I wanted to get  this on the air is we really wanted to  give this family something that they  have not gotten up to now particularly  Skylar Richardson the presumption of  innocence looking at the case as it is  and it's a complicated case and it's an  emotional tough case yeah you do wonder  I mean everybody when is when they when  when you hear that someone didn't know  they were pregnant but you look at those  pictures and and you get it that's why  we put that because it's seven and a  half months she's wearing a two-piece  and her parents when you have someone  without eating disorder you're afraid to  talk about weight yeah and they didn't  want to keep bringing up they thought  she looked healthy one of the things  that really troubled me the most about  this case was this pretrial publicity it  was so negative it was so prejudicial it  was social media oh yes it was amplified  and was inaccurate the prosecuting  attorney went public with inflammatory  remarks that later turned out to be  totally wrong but then they were  amplified by social media these these  people have gotten death threats how  Scott are doing well she's doing better  than I mean what she was before she is  now enrolled in a new eating disorder  program she's working at the lawyer's  office where she has been working and  she's hoping to start college in January  all right Erin thank you they're in  Moriarty
 

